In summary, while Dickens wrote within the cultural norms and prejudices of his time, his depictions of Jewish characters continue to be subjects of debate and analysis in the realms of literary criticism and antisemitism. The extent to which he perpetuated antisemitic stereotypes remains a complex topic open to scholarly interpretation. 

